{"lines":[{"y":0.033430232413812155,"w":0.12139918009440104,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"Audioscripts","x":0.088477364574664541},{"y":0.078488372281805607,"h":0.014562275440588968,"c":1,"w":0.73868311564127609,"t":"Seneca and Marcus Aurelius. Amazingly, we still have access to these ideas, despite the fact","x":0.090534991733545567},{"y":0.094476744053032746,"t":"that the most famous Stoics never wrote anything down for publication. Cato definitely didn't.","h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.73662551879882809,"x":0.08847736397181194},{"w":0.73670593261718753,"t":"Marcus Aurelius never intended his Meditations to be anything but personal. Seneca's letters","h":0.015767777626028656,"x":0.090496790872430025,"y":0.10885867210607503,"c":1},{"t":"were, well, letters and Epictetus' thoughts come to us by way of a note-taking student.","c":1,"h":0.018728629719944268,"w":0.68528213500976565,"x":0.088416103275951813,"y":0.12248174786355481},{"y":0.14811542994160332,"w":0.66255142211914053,"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.088477375255999816,"t":"Stoic principles were based on the idea that its followers could have an unshakable","c":1},{"t":"happiness in this life and the key to achieving this was virtue. The road to virtue, in turn, lay","h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1,"x":0.088477380971599184,"w":0.72633743286132812,"y":0.16279069789253287},{"c":1,"y":0.1771623802935377,"h":0.01759625829150735,"x":0.090461955483714579,"t":"in understanding that destructive emotions, like anger and jealousy, are under our conscious","w":0.73471247355143221},{"w":0.71604939778645837,"x":0.090534971791910834,"y":0.19464075357781363,"t":"control - they don't have to control us, because we can learn to control them. In the words","c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132},{"x":0.088477379048374119,"t":"of Epictetus: \"external events I cannot control, but the choices I make with regard to them,","y":0.20784883746738747,"h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1,"w":0.71604934692382805},{"h":0.014560564106288698,"y":0.22526501740421279,"w":0.10493827184041342,"t":"1 do controỊi","x":0.088477366025770013,"c":1},{"x":0.090534987147055879,"h":0.013100227562642619,"c":1,"t":"The modern day philosopher and writer Nassim Nicholas Taleb defines a Stoic as someone","y":0.24852767952936028,"w":0.72633743286132812},{"c":1,"w":0.68518519083658858,"y":0.26295641933108016,"t":"who has a different perspective on experiences which most of us would see as wholly","h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.088477357488084371},{"y":0.27906976730821698,"h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1,"t":"negative; a Stoic \"transforms fear into caution, pain into transformation, mistakes into","x":0.088477356107467528,"w":0.6769547526041666},{"w":0.69135803222656245,"h":0.014558851087051128,"c":1,"t":"initiation and desire into undertaking\". Using this definition as a model, we can see that","y":0.29358068318395336,"x":0.090534974164496587},{"w":0.67923823038736986,"x":0.090428920618367103,"y":0.30807294433060217,"h":0.017546511651208685,"t":"throughout the centuries Stoicism has been practised in more recent history by kings,","c":1},{"c":1,"t":"presidents, artists, writers and entrepreneurs.","w":0.36419754028320311,"y":0.32558139522152119,"x":0.090534974503997598,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.094476744030018045,"t":"Q32","w":0.037037035624186143,"x":0.860082305124242,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"y":0.20930232542296223,"w":0.037037035624186254,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"Q33","x":0.86008230513029349},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"t":"Q34","w":0.037037035624186143,"y":0.26308139515860907,"x":0.86008230521031204},{"t":"The founding fathers of the United States were inspired by the philosophy. George","w":0.65236658732096353,"x":0.092533776719672958,"y":0.36907997291888905,"h":0.014624985424172121,"c":1},{"t":"Washington was introduced to Stoicism by his neighbours at age seventeen, and later, put on","x":0.092592581172208005,"y":0.38515901084656856,"w":0.74074076334635419,"h":0.01455029160732102,"c":1},{"w":0.73055053710937501,"x":0.090492077076342339,"h":0.016039266462741675,"t":"a play based on the life of Cato to inspire his men. Thomas Jefferson kept a copy of Seneca","y":0.39846497875165021,"c":1},{"t":"besıde his bed.","c":1,"x":0.090534981356260716,"h":0.011627907185728592,"y":0.41715116267582342,"w":0.12551439921061197},{"c":1,"t":"Writers and artists have also been inspired by the stoics. Eugène Delacroix, the renowned","h":0.013081395583944611,"w":0.71604939778645837,"y":0.43895348825199432,"x":0.09053497175015518},{"x":0.088477378699732587,"c":1,"h":0.014534883982160851,"y":0.45494186033210249,"t":"French Romantic artist (known best for his painting Liberty Leading the People) was an","w":0.69547322591145833},{"t":"ardent Stoic, referring to it as his \"consoling religion\".","x":0.090534988865027324,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.46790341594783191,"w":0.42181068420410162},{"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.69753087361653643,"y":0.49263839810504784,"x":0.090534974921596553,"t":"The economist Adam Smith's theories on capitalism were significantly influenced by the","c":1},{"t":"Stoicism that he studied as a schoolboy, under a teacher who had translated Marcus Aurelius'","y":0.50724708483397463,"w":0.74700246175130214,"x":0.090500391653644097,"h":0.015190339060357605,"c":1},{"t":"works.","y":0.52333552820532703,"x":0.087769256616339414,"c":1,"w":0.059198716481526692,"h":0.014890157432241535},{"c":1,"y":0.54796511614639576,"t":"Today's political leaders are no different, with many finding their inspiration from the ancient","x":0.08847735673296625,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.72839508056640634},{"h":0.014932288719150311,"t":"texts. Former US president Bill Clinton rereads Marcus Aurelius every single year, and many","x":0.088427645822404671,"y":0.56120082999839971,"w":0.73468846638997398,"c":1},{"t":"have compared former President Obama's calm leadership style to that of Cato. Wen Jiabao,","c":1,"x":0.090434360720773557,"y":0.57540728344155767,"w":0.74095621744791662,"h":0.017652594720236059},{"y":0.59302325566705327,"w":0.74691360473632806,"h":0.015988372380376759,"c":1,"t":"the former prime minister of China, claims that Meditations is one of two books he travels with","x":0.088477353872294578},{"y":0.60661072272516048,"t":"and that he has read it more than one hundred times over the course of his life.","w":0.63183837890625005,"x":0.090474286796665151,"h":0.015530436844932383,"c":1},{"w":0.74279836018880208,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"y":0.63221436958347876,"t":"Stoicism had a profound influence on Albert Ellis, who invented Cognitive Behaviour Therapy,","x":0.088477363005224283},{"t":"which is used to help people manage their problems by changing the way that they think and","w":0.73868311564127609,"x":0.088477372119392231,"y":0.6481154299285411,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.088477366739462673,"y":0.66279069754011422,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.71810699462890626,"t":"behave. It's most commonly used to treat depression. The idea is that we can take control"},{"y":0.67873969378141419,"w":0.73251027425130211,"c":1,"t":"of our lives by challenging the irrational beliefs that create our faulty thinking, symptoms and","x":0.088477373060999676,"h":0.014574259835502756},{"w":0.27599484761555987,"y":0.69324372154731706,"t":"behaviours by using logic instead.","x":0.088334858236318425,"c":1,"h":0.01557785658729649},{"x":0.092592586798160043,"h":0.013250883392226243,"y":0.71643109532533233,"w":0.70370371500651041,"c":1,"t":"Stoicism has also become popular in the world of business. Stoic principles can build the"},{"c":1,"h":0.015172739332219298,"y":0.73050625637758759,"w":0.70795232137044273,"x":0.090484017827578977,"t":"resilience and state of mind required to overcome setbacks because Stoics teach turning"},{"h":0.011778563015312105,"c":1,"t":"obstacles into opportunity. A lesson every business entrepreneur needs to learn.","x":0.090534974919675854,"y":0.74852767954267685,"w":0.63991770426432282},{"t":"I would argue that studying Stoicism is as relevant today as it was 2,000 years ago, thanks to","h":0.014546867815428799,"c":1,"x":0.088477363011149918,"w":0.74279836018880208,"y":0.77179034161547078},{"x":0.086419741671322464,"y":0.78621908103454008,"w":0.74074076334635419,"t":"its brilliant insights into how to lead a good life. At the very root of the thinking, there is a very","h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"w":0.037037035624186143,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"Q35","y":0.38517441845076017,"c":1,"x":0.86008230513029371},{"y":0.49273255798110183,"t":"Q36","x":0.86008230513029349,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"w":0.037037035624186254},{"c":1,"x":0.86008230513029371,"y":0.63226744170657423,"t":"Q37","w":0.037037035624186143,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"x":0.860082305124242,"t":"Q38","y":0.67877906961141354,"w":0.037037035624186143,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1},{"y":0.73255813937645065,"w":0.037037035624186254,"c":1,"x":0.86008230513029349,"t":"Q39","h":0.013081395583944611},{"t":"Q40","x":0.86008230513029349,"y":0.78633720914389238,"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.037037035624186254,"c":1},{"w":0.037037035624186185,"t":"102","x":0.090534980027413073,"y":0.90552325565552039,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"h":0.027081890577983492,"y":0.95559854902539954,"x":0.71952531067331094,"w":0.25427068074544268,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","c":1}],"w":2400,"h":3396}